# VANTERA PLATFORM — CURSOR RULES
# Read this before generating any file.
# These rules are non-negotiable and apply to every file in this project.

## WHO WE ARE BUILDING
Vantera is a white-label multi-tenant business operations platform.
It connects existing business tools (HubSpot, QuickBooks, AppFolio)
and provides native replacements for businesses that don't have them.
Every client-facing surface is branded to the business — never to Vantera.

## TECH STACK (exact imports only — no alternatives)
- Framework:        Next.js 14 App Router
- Language:         TypeScript strict mode — .ts and .tsx only
- Styling:          Tailwind CSS utility classes only
- Components:       shadcn/ui — extend, never replace
- State (server):   TanStack Query (@tanstack/react-query)
- State (client):   Zustand
- Forms:            React Hook Form + Zod (@hookform/resolvers/zod)
- Tables:           TanStack Table (@tanstack/react-table)
- Drag/drop:        @dnd-kit/core + @dnd-kit/sortable
- Database:         Drizzle ORM (drizzle-orm/pg-core) — import from @vantera/db
- DB client:        import { db } from '@/lib/db/client' — never instantiate inline
- Auth:             Supabase Auth via @supabase/ssr
- Jobs:             Trigger.dev (@trigger.dev/sdk)
- Email:            Resend + React Email (@react-email/components)
- SMS:              Twilio (twilio)
- Payments:         Stripe (stripe + @stripe/stripe-js)
- AI:               Anthropic via Vercel AI SDK (ai + @ai-sdk/anthropic)
- Animation:        Framer Motion (framer-motion)
- Charts:           Recharts (recharts)
- Icons:            Lucide React (lucide-react) — no other icon library
- Dates:            date-fns — no moment.js, no dayjs
- HTTP client:      Native fetch only — no axios in components

## ABSOLUTE RULES — NEVER VIOLATE

### Multi-Tenancy (most critical)
- EVERY database query must filter by accountId
- Pattern: .where(and(eq(table.accountId, accountId), isNull(table.deletedAt)))
- accountId ALWAYS comes from the validated session — never from URL, query params, or request body
- If you write a query without accountId filter: it is a critical security bug

### Soft Deletes
- NEVER call db.delete() on any table
- All deletes: await db.update(table).set({ deletedAt: new Date() }).where(...)
- All list queries: must include isNull(table.deletedAt) in the where clause
- Tables without deletedAt (activities, automation_runs): these are immutable logs — never delete

### Branding
- The string "Vantera" must NEVER appear in:
  app/(portal)/ — any file
  Any email template
  Any SMS template body
  Any page <title> rendered to a contact
  Any default value for business name, logo, or color
- Brand values ALWAYS come from: const { businessName, primaryColor, logoUrl } = useBranding()
- In server components: const branding = getBrandingFromHeaders(headers())

### Session Rules
- Admin sessions: userId + accountId + role — access /admin/* only
- Portal sessions: contactId + accountId — access /portal/* only
- These never overlap — no shared session store, no shared cookies
- Cookie names: v_admin_session and v_portal_session
- Always validate session with: const session = await requireAdminSession()
  or: const session = await requirePortalSession()
- If session.accountId !== resolved accountId from middleware: reject immediately

### AI Output
- Team plan: Claude output NEVER sent to contacts without template wrapping or human review
- Enterprise plan: autonomous send only when evaluateFlag('autonomous_ai_messaging') === true
- Never log Claude responses containing contact PII

## CODE PATTERNS — USE EXACTLY

### Server Action
```ts
export async function actionName(input: z.infer<typeof inputSchema>) {
  const session = await requireAdminSession()
  const validated = inputSchema.parse(input)
  try {
    const result = await db.transaction(async (tx) => {
      // multi-table writes go here
    })
    return { success: true, data: result }
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('[actionName]', error)
    return { success: false, error: 'Operation failed' }
  }
}
```

### Drizzle Query (list)
```ts
const results = await db.query.tableName.findMany({
  where: and(
    eq(tableName.accountId, session.accountId),
    isNull(tableName.deletedAt)
  ),
  orderBy: desc(tableName.createdAt),
  limit: 50,
})
```

### Drizzle Query (single)
```ts
const record = await db.query.tableName.findFirst({
  where: and(
    eq(tableName.id, id),
    eq(tableName.accountId, session.accountId),
    isNull(tableName.deletedAt)
  ),
})
if (!record) return { success: false, error: 'Not found' }
```

### Soft Delete
```ts
await db
  .update(tableName)
  .set({ deletedAt: new Date() })
  .where(and(
    eq(tableName.id, id),
    eq(tableName.accountId, session.accountId)
  ))
```

### API Response Shape (always)
```ts
{ success: true, data: T }
{ success: false, error: string, code?: string }
```

### React Hook Form + Zod
```ts
const form = useForm<z.infer<typeof formSchema>>({
  resolver: zodResolver(formSchema),
  defaultValues: { ... },
})
```

### Feature Flag Check (server)
```ts
const isEnabled = await evaluateFlag({
  accountId: session.accountId,
  plan: session.plan,
  flagName: 'feature_name'
})
if (!isEnabled) return { success: false, error: 'Feature not available', code: 'FEATURE_GATED' }
```

## FILE CONVENTIONS

### File naming
- Components: PascalCase.tsx (RecordBoard.tsx, ContactProfile.tsx)
- Hooks: camelCase with use prefix (useRecords.ts, useContacts.ts)
- Actions: actions.ts — colocated with route segment
- Types: types.ts — colocated with feature
- Schemas: schema.ts — colocated with feature
- Constants: constants.ts — colocated if feature-specific, lib/constants.ts if shared
- Utils: lib/utils/featureName.ts

### Component rules
- One component per file — named export matches filename exactly
- "use client" only when: useState, useEffect, useRef, browser APIs, event handlers
- Server Components fetch their own data — no prop drilling of server data
- Client Components receive data as props or use TanStack Query
- No business logic inside components — extract to lib/ functions
- Loading states: use Suspense boundaries + skeleton components from shadcn
- Empty states: every list view has an empty state component
- Error states: every async operation has an error state

### Import order (auto-formatted but enforce mentally)
1. React and Next.js
2. Third-party libraries
3. Internal packages (@vantera/db, @vantera/types)
4. Internal aliases (@/lib, @/components, @/app)
5. Relative imports

## MONOREPO STRUCTURE
- Package manager: pnpm only — never npm install or yarn add
- apps/web/app/(admin)  — admin route group
- apps/web/app/(portal) — client portal route group
- apps/web/app/(auth)   — auth routes
- apps/web/app/api      — API routes and webhooks
- packages/db           — Drizzle schema and migrations (source of truth)
- packages/types        — shared TypeScript types
- packages/utils        — shared utilities

## COMMANDS
```bash
pnpm dev          # turbo dev (all packages)
pnpm build        # turbo build
pnpm lint         # turbo lint
pnpm type-check   # turbo type-check
pnpm db:generate  # drizzle-kit generate
pnpm db:migrate   # drizzle-kit migrate
pnpm db:push      # drizzle-kit push
pnpm db:studio    # drizzle-kit studio
```

## WHAT CURSOR MUST NEVER DO
- Never use Pages Router (no getServerSideProps, getStaticProps, _app.tsx)
- Never use axios in components — use fetch or TanStack Query
- Never use useState for form values — always React Hook Form
- Never hardcode accountId, userId, or contactId values
- Never write db.delete() — soft deletes only
- Never use any CSS module files — Tailwind only
- Never use styled-components or emotion
- Never use moment.js or dayjs — use date-fns
- Never install a package not in the approved stack without flagging it
- Never write a query without accountId — this is a multi-tenant security requirement
- Never put the word "Vantera" in any portal-facing component
- Never expose database error messages in API responses
- Never skip loading and error states in components
